1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,230
Nigga, it’s my motherfucking funeral.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,560
The man taking tickets didn’t look up.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,109
Forty dollars.

4
00:00:06,349 --> 00:00:11,949
I’m Aiden. He looked at me. Looked at the six-foot photograph beside
the door. Looked back.

5
00:00:12,129 --> 00:00:14,092
You look better in the picture.

6
00:00:14,392 --> 00:00:15,992
Nigga, I’m alive.

7
00:00:16,112 --> 00:00:17,605
Then you can pay.

8
00:00:18,055 --> 00:00:35,095
Vegas. After the homecoming. I had been back long enough for these
niggas to start charging admission to my problems. Somebody had put
angel wings on a photograph of me getting arrested. Cropped out the
cuffs, left the officer’s hand on my shoulder. Nigga had a police
escort into heaven. I called Tank.

9
00:00:35,295 --> 00:00:37,855
Why there a cover charge at my funeral?

10
00:00:37,955 --> 00:00:40,035
The shrimp was expensive.

11
00:00:40,215 --> 00:00:42,135
Why do I have shrimp?

12
00:00:42,235 --> 00:00:43,915
You died successful.

13
00:00:44,245 --> 00:00:47,925
I heard chewing. Nigga, are you eating?

14
00:00:48,025 --> 00:00:48,905
Grieving.

15
00:00:49,405 --> 00:00:53,245
I paid the forty. The nigga stamped DECEASED on my wrist.

16
00:00:53,395 --> 00:00:55,486
That gets you one well drink.

17
00:00:55,586 --> 00:00:59,346
One? Nigga, the sign says two-drink minimum.

18
00:00:59,496 --> 00:01:01,949
Second one’s your responsibility.

19
00:01:02,299 --> 00:01:04,059
A nigga behind me shook his head.

20
00:01:04,179 --> 00:01:06,723
Hold up. Ain’t that the deceased?

21
00:01:06,843 --> 00:01:08,683
Ticket man looked at my stamp.

22
00:01:08,803 --> 00:01:10,169
Paid deceased.

23
00:01:10,499 --> 00:01:12,179
The nigga pulled out his phone.

24
00:01:12,279 --> 00:01:13,984
Can I get a picture?

25
00:01:14,084 --> 00:01:15,044
Of me alive?

26
00:01:15,144 --> 00:01:17,832
People gonna think I knew you personally.

27
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:20,112
Nigga, you meeting me personally.

28
00:01:20,232 --> 00:01:22,963
Yeah, but the funeral picture hit different.

29
00:01:23,313 --> 00:01:24,913
I kept walking.

30
00:01:25,563 --> 00:01:29,643
Shawna found me beside the chocolate fountain, turning my memorial
program upside down.

31
00:01:29,793 --> 00:01:32,833
Why this say I’m survived by eleven children?

32
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:34,260
Those are sponsors.

33
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:36,900
Nigga, one of them’s Jeremiah.

34
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,923
Jeremiah’s Collision Repair.

35
00:01:39,283 --> 00:01:47,123
My wife looked beautiful in black. Slit up one leg, diamond at her
throat, hat tilted like she had already forgiven herself. You enjoying
widowhood?

36
00:01:47,243 --> 00:01:48,824
The parking is excellent.

37
00:01:49,174 --> 00:01:53,494
I pulled her close. She put two fingers against my mouth.

38
00:01:53,594 --> 00:01:57,093
Eight minutes. Kitchen. Stay there until we get the case.

39
00:01:57,273 --> 00:02:00,473
Nigga, I could take it right now.

40
00:02:00,573 --> 00:02:04,998
And Silas’s men could start shooting into everybody who paid to eat
shrimp.

41
00:02:05,158 --> 00:02:06,838
Apparently excellent shrimp.

42
00:02:07,018 --> 00:02:07,914
Aiden.

43
00:02:08,214 --> 00:02:34,054
I straightened up. Mercedes stood beside the stage in a red suit,
thumb pressed into her palm. She’d been doing that all week. Silas
Gold had stolen the original recordings of her first album. The nigga
had locked the drive in a silver case and invited buyers to bid. She
could sing every song again. She couldn’t rebuild the demolished
studio, recall every musician to the same night, or make her voice
crack exactly where it had in the last chorus. She had left that crack
in. Said it sounded like her.

44
00:02:34,504 --> 00:02:54,584
Silas lived behind bulletproof glass and sent other niggas out to be
unpleasant. Tell him Aiden was dead, though, and suddenly the
motherfucker wanted fresh air. Shawna had promised a private auction
after the memorial. My watch, my cars, the collection. Silas would
bring the recordings so they could settle everything together.
Mercedes would inspect the case backstage. Porsche would switch it. I
would stay in the fucking kitchen.

45
00:02:55,004 --> 00:02:58,204
Mercedes caught me looking and came to fix my collar.

46
00:02:58,324 --> 00:02:59,939
Nigga, don’t do the thing.

47
00:03:00,099 --> 00:03:01,059
Which thing?

48
00:03:01,209 --> 00:03:02,969
She looked around my funeral.

49
00:03:03,069 --> 00:03:05,081
The thing where this becomes about you.

50
00:03:05,261 --> 00:03:07,021
My photograph is six feet tall.

51
00:03:07,121 --> 00:03:09,904
Exactly. The nigga has enough publicity.

52
00:03:10,224 --> 00:03:13,024
I stopped smiling. You’ll get your music.

53
00:03:13,174 --> 00:03:15,450
I know. I want to enjoy getting it.

54
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:19,650
She squeezed my shoulder and went back to the stage. Shawna kissed me.

55
00:03:19,790 --> 00:03:20,686
Kitchen.

56
00:03:20,926 --> 00:03:24,446
Nigga, y’all got one word for me tonight. She turned me toward the
door.

57
00:03:25,096 --> 00:03:31,336
They had hired a full band. Horns, two keyboards, drummer wearing
sunglasses he hadn’t removed for either prayer.

58
00:03:31,516 --> 00:03:34,556
Tank took the microphone carrying a plate.

59
00:03:34,736 --> 00:03:39,456
We gathered here because my brother would want these niggas supporting
the bar.

60
00:03:39,656 --> 00:03:41,576
Glasses went up.

61
00:03:41,756 --> 00:03:45,836
Aiden was generous. Nigga gave me the shirt off his back.

62
00:03:46,036 --> 00:03:48,516
I leaned toward the kitchen speaker.

63
00:03:48,696 --> 00:03:51,736
Police was looking for a man in a red shirt.

64
00:03:51,916 --> 00:03:53,276
The room broke open.

65
00:03:53,456 --> 00:03:57,776
I pushed through the kitchen door. Shawna held up one finger without
turning around.

66
00:03:57,956 --> 00:03:59,156
Back I went.

67
00:03:59,336 --> 00:04:01,256
But my nigga came back,

68
00:04:01,456 --> 00:04:02,976
Tank said.

69
00:04:03,156 --> 00:04:04,276
The room quieted.

70
00:04:04,456 --> 00:04:11,656
Came to the station. Told them I hadn’t done shit. Paid everything.
Waited six hours. Bought me breakfast.

71
00:04:11,856 --> 00:04:13,936
My palm rested against the door.

72
00:04:14,116 --> 00:04:15,316
Tank sniffed.

73
00:04:15,496 --> 00:04:17,496
Then the nigga asked for his shirt.

74
00:04:17,696 --> 00:04:22,336
The drummer caught the laugh with a roll. I had to smile. Nigga knew
when to hit.

75
00:04:22,516 --> 00:04:24,276
Then somebody booed.

76
00:04:24,456 --> 00:04:37,416
Silas Gold entered in a white fur coat. Four men followed him.
Smallest nigga carried the silver case. Biggest had a neck wider than
my thigh and an expression like somebody assembled him without the
last page.

77
00:04:37,596 --> 00:04:39,596
Silas raised a bottle.

78
00:04:39,776 --> 00:04:41,438
Miss the good part?

79
00:04:41,638 --> 00:04:44,198
Tank looked at the closed coffin.

80
00:04:44,378 --> 00:04:47,018
Depends how this speech goes.

81
00:04:47,218 --> 00:04:50,098
Silas laughed. His niggas joined a second late.

82
00:04:50,278 --> 00:04:55,958
Shawna offered her hand. He bent to kiss it. She moved it just enough
that his mouth met his own thumb.

83
00:04:56,138 --> 00:04:57,297
The recordings.

84
00:04:57,497 --> 00:04:59,418
After my tribute.

85
00:04:59,618 --> 00:05:02,467
Mercedes inspects them first. We agreed.

86
00:05:02,667 --> 00:05:06,267
Darling, look at the crowd. Can’t buy timing.

87
00:05:06,467 --> 00:05:10,387
He took the microphone from Tank and balanced his bottle on my coffin.

88
00:05:10,567 --> 00:05:11,607
Tank handed it back.

89
00:05:11,787 --> 00:05:13,947
Silas put it down.

90
00:05:14,127 --> 00:05:15,647
Tank handed it back.

91
00:05:15,827 --> 00:05:18,547
The drummer gave them a little tick, tick, tick.

92
00:05:18,727 --> 00:05:20,727
Silas stopped smiling.

93
00:05:20,907 --> 00:05:23,127
You got somewhere to be?

94
00:05:23,327 --> 00:05:25,247
Nigga, eventually.

95
00:05:25,447 --> 00:05:27,367
Silas faced the crowd.

96
00:05:27,547 --> 00:05:30,164
Aiden and I had differences.

97
00:05:30,364 --> 00:05:34,364
From the kitchen I mouthed, Nigga, you stole my boat.

98
00:05:34,544 --> 00:05:36,974
But he was a man of appetite.

99
00:05:37,174 --> 00:05:38,534
He looked at Shawna.

100
00:05:38,714 --> 00:05:44,439
Appetite leaves things unfinished. People unprovided for. I would
never presume—

101
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:45,671
Then don’t.

102
00:05:45,871 --> 00:05:48,351
A woman slapped her table.

103
00:05:48,531 --> 00:05:50,247
That nigga got instructions!

104
00:05:50,447 --> 00:05:53,887
Silas waited out the laughter with his teeth showing.

105
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:56,423
Mercedes. Up here.

106
00:05:56,623 --> 00:05:57,983
She didn’t move.

107
00:05:58,163 --> 00:06:02,803
The case opened. Silas put his bottle on the coffin and took out the
hard drive.

108
00:06:02,983 --> 00:06:09,184
Perhaps our little lady could sing a tribute. And apologize for some
things she’s said about me.

109
00:06:09,384 --> 00:06:11,304
Mercedes walked toward the steps.

110
00:06:11,484 --> 00:06:13,047
You promised an inspection.

111
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:14,611
Sing first.

112
00:06:14,811 --> 00:06:19,531
The biggest nigga blocked the backstage doorway. Porsche stood behind
him with the duplicate case.

113
00:06:19,711 --> 00:06:23,551
Silas offered Mercedes the microphone. Pulled it back.

114
00:06:23,731 --> 00:06:25,141
Ask nicely.

115
00:06:25,341 --> 00:06:26,861
I took off my jacket.

116
00:06:27,041 --> 00:06:29,281
The cook looked up from his potatoes.

117
00:06:29,461 --> 00:06:31,283
Nigga, you want me to hold that?

118
00:06:31,483 --> 00:06:32,203
Please.

119
00:06:32,383 --> 00:06:33,577
You coming back?

120
00:06:33,777 --> 00:06:35,377
I looked through the round window.

121
00:06:35,557 --> 00:06:36,917
Apparently I do.

122
00:06:37,567 --> 00:06:39,647
I walked out carrying shrimp.

123
00:06:39,827 --> 00:06:44,947
Shawna saw my hands, looked at the stage, and shifted her chair clear
of the aisle.

124
00:06:45,127 --> 00:06:46,807
Tank set down his plate.

125
00:06:46,987 --> 00:06:49,867
A woman near the aisle looked from me to the coffin.

126
00:06:50,047 --> 00:06:51,147
Lord.

127
00:06:51,347 --> 00:06:53,667
The nigga beside her crossed himself.

128
00:06:53,847 --> 00:06:55,106
Don't do that,

129
00:06:55,306 --> 00:06:56,586
she whispered.

130
00:06:56,766 --> 00:06:58,469
He got shrimp.

131
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:00,458
Could still be spiritual.

132
00:07:00,658 --> 00:07:02,578
Nigga, move your chair.

133
00:07:02,758 --> 00:07:06,919
They moved. I passed between them without losing a shrimp.

134
00:07:07,098 --> 00:07:11,098
From the stage, the drummer lifted one stick and watched me approach.

135
00:07:11,278 --> 00:07:13,598
I stopped beside the smallest nigga.

136
00:07:13,778 --> 00:07:14,818
Shrimp?

137
00:07:14,998 --> 00:07:15,798
He took one.

138
00:07:15,978 --> 00:07:16,858
Sauce?

139
00:07:17,038 --> 00:07:17,998
He nodded.

140
00:07:18,178 --> 00:07:19,858
Help yourself, my nigga.

141
00:07:20,038 --> 00:07:24,678
Silas heard me. Turned so fast the fur collar slapped his mouth.

142
00:07:24,858 --> 00:07:26,218
He stared.

143
00:07:26,398 --> 00:07:29,358
Forty dollars. Worth it.

144
00:07:29,538 --> 00:07:30,089
You—

145
00:07:30,289 --> 00:07:32,769
Nigga, it’s my motherfucking funeral.

146
00:07:32,949 --> 00:07:36,309
He shoved the microphone into its stand and reached inside his coat.

147
00:07:36,489 --> 00:07:49,449
I drove the tray under his wrist. The pistol fired through the
ceiling, flew from his hand, and skidded under the piano. Plaster
burst over the stage. The trumpet player ducked. Tank tackled two
guests behind a table without spilling his drink.

148
00:07:49,629 --> 00:07:51,709
I caught Silas by the coat.

149
00:07:51,889 --> 00:07:55,009
Nigga, everybody else brought flowers!

150
00:07:55,189 --> 00:08:01,029
He grabbed his bottle from the coffin and swung. Glass broke against
my shoulder. Pain ran down my arm.

151
00:08:01,209 --> 00:08:02,499
Motherfucker.

152
00:08:02,699 --> 00:08:04,219
I hit him with the tray.

153
00:08:04,399 --> 00:08:08,479
The drive flew from his other hand. Mercedes caught it against her
chest.

154
00:08:08,659 --> 00:08:09,454
Got it!

155
00:08:09,654 --> 00:08:16,854
The biggest nigga lunged. Porsche hooked his ankle with the duplicate
case. He stumbled down the steps into the chair Shawna had picked up.

156
00:08:17,034 --> 00:08:19,034
The chair lost.

157
00:08:19,214 --> 00:08:20,654
So did his teeth.

158
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,834
He sat carefully among the pieces.

159
00:08:23,014 --> 00:08:23,846
Stay,

160
00:08:24,046 --> 00:08:25,726
my wife said.

161
00:08:25,906 --> 00:08:27,586
Nigga stayed.

162
00:08:27,766 --> 00:08:37,606
Mercedes tucked the drive inside her jacket. Behind me, another man
drew a gun. I saw him in the mirrored wall and ducked as she threw the
microphone stand over my head with both hands.

163
00:08:37,786 --> 00:08:40,826
It hit the nigga across the chest and carried him into the drum kit.

164
00:08:41,006 --> 00:08:43,566
The crash filled the room.

165
00:08:43,746 --> 00:08:48,946
The drummer stood. Looked at his broken cymbal. Looked at the man
under it.

166
00:08:49,126 --> 00:08:50,833
Nigga, that’s vintage.

167
00:08:51,033 --> 00:08:52,713
Then he hit him with the stool.

168
00:08:52,893 --> 00:09:00,333
Silas wriggled free of his coat. Ran for the steps. Tank caught him
around the waist, flung open the coffin with his free hand, and tipped
him inside.

169
00:09:00,513 --> 00:09:02,913
The coffin rocked. Lid banged shut.

170
00:09:03,093 --> 00:09:04,453
Something squealed.

171
00:09:04,633 --> 00:09:06,233
Tank froze.

172
00:09:06,413 --> 00:09:06,973
Shit.

173
00:09:07,173 --> 00:09:08,373
The lid flew up.

174
00:09:08,553 --> 00:09:15,353
A little man in a gold tracksuit sat upright underneath Silas, wearing
my spare sunglasses and looking ready to fight the entire funeral.

175
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:17,390
NIGGA, I TOLD YOU NINE-FIFTEEN!

176
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:19,350
I stared at Tank.

177
00:09:19,530 --> 00:09:21,130
Tank stared at his shoes.

178
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:23,310
You hired a corpse?

179
00:09:23,490 --> 00:09:25,250
Resurrection package.

180
00:09:25,450 --> 00:09:26,570
Nigga.

181
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:28,510
It included the dance.

182
00:09:28,710 --> 00:09:30,630
The little man pointed at Tank.

183
00:09:30,810 --> 00:09:31,778
And fog.

184
00:09:31,978 --> 00:09:34,698
Tank pointed at the dust hanging over the stage.

185
00:09:34,878 --> 00:09:37,038
Nigga, we got atmosphere.

186
00:09:37,238 --> 00:09:38,313
That’s ceiling.

187
00:09:38,513 --> 00:09:40,353
Nigga, work with the venue.

188
00:09:40,553 --> 00:09:43,913
The little man climbed over Silas’s stomach and straightened his
tracksuit.

189
00:09:44,093 --> 00:09:48,916
I do the surprise. I do the dance. I leave. Ain’t no nigga mentioned
wrestling.

190
00:09:49,116 --> 00:09:53,836
Silas’s fourth man backed toward the exit. Tank pointed at him without
looking away from me.

191
00:09:54,016 --> 00:09:56,736
Sit your ass down. The nigga hasn’t danced.

192
00:09:56,936 --> 00:09:57,896
He sat.

193
00:09:58,076 --> 00:10:03,276
The smallest man still held the empty case and a shrimp tail. He
lowered the case very slowly.

194
00:10:03,456 --> 00:10:04,776
I’m with catering.

195
00:10:04,976 --> 00:10:06,016
From the kitchen:

196
00:10:06,196 --> 00:10:07,763
No the fuck you are not.

197
00:10:08,413 --> 00:10:14,093
Seven minutes to collect the guns, tie up Silas’s men, and convince
everybody the bar remained open.

198
00:10:14,273 --> 00:10:19,473
Silas kept trying to sit up in the coffin. The little man eased him
down with a sneaker against his forehead.

199
00:10:19,653 --> 00:10:22,010
Stop touching my face.

200
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:23,983
Stop being in my office, nigga.

201
00:10:24,183 --> 00:10:32,023
At the sound desk, Mercedes took the drive from her jacket and plugged
it in. Files appeared. She chose one, listened through the headphones,
and closed her eyes.

202
00:10:32,203 --> 00:10:34,603
Porsche took her hand beneath the table.

203
00:10:34,783 --> 00:10:38,063
I moved closer. Shawna caught my belt and pulled me back.

204
00:10:38,243 --> 00:10:39,283
We waited.

205
00:10:39,463 --> 00:10:42,823
Mercedes removed the headphones and wiped under one eye.

206
00:10:43,003 --> 00:10:43,788
All here.

207
00:10:43,988 --> 00:10:45,348
Tank breathed out.

208
00:10:45,528 --> 00:10:47,608
Then play one, my nigga.

209
00:10:47,808 --> 00:10:55,568
She looked around. Overturned flowers. Two men bleeding into memorial
napkins. My giant face leaning crookedly against the wall.

210
00:10:55,748 --> 00:10:57,188
Then she went to the stage.

211
00:10:57,368 --> 00:10:59,448
The drummer was fitting a spare cymbal.

212
00:10:59,628 --> 00:11:00,443
You good?

213
00:11:00,643 --> 00:11:02,530
You doing something slow?

214
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:03,416
No.

215
00:11:03,616 --> 00:11:04,336
He sat.

216
00:11:04,516 --> 00:11:05,721
Then yeah.

217
00:11:05,921 --> 00:11:14,081
She gave the sound man a track number. A hiss came through the
speakers, then saxophone, warm and rough. The band found its rhythm.

218
00:11:14,261 --> 00:11:16,181
Mercedes pointed at my portrait.

219
00:11:16,361 --> 00:11:18,931
Turn that nigga around. I need the room.

220
00:11:19,131 --> 00:11:20,491
I turned it myself.

221
00:11:20,671 --> 00:11:32,111
She sang low at first, almost speaking. Bass came underneath. She
planted a heel against the monitor and let the next line climb. By the
chorus, people stood between fallen chairs finding somebody to dance
with.

222
00:11:32,291 --> 00:11:35,331
The little man shut the coffin and started dancing on it.

223
00:11:35,511 --> 00:11:36,570
Get off!

224
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:38,290
Silas shouted.

225
00:11:38,470 --> 00:11:39,744
Nine-fifteen, bitch!

226
00:11:39,944 --> 00:11:41,544
Tank raised both hands.

227
00:11:41,724 --> 00:11:44,045
That nigga earned his deposit!

228
00:11:44,244 --> 00:11:54,004
Porsche laughed with her face turned up. The cook came out with my
jacket over his shoulder and a tray in his hands. A woman took the
tray, put it on a table, and pulled him onto the floor.

229
00:11:54,184 --> 00:11:55,724
Nigga, I’m working.

230
00:11:55,924 --> 00:11:57,298
Not anymore.

231
00:11:57,498 --> 00:11:59,738
Shawna slipped her fingers into mine.

232
00:11:59,918 --> 00:12:00,984
You’re bleeding.

233
00:12:01,184 --> 00:12:02,304
Little bit.

234
00:12:02,484 --> 00:12:05,444
She touched my sleeve. I winced.

235
00:12:05,624 --> 00:12:06,938
We’ll get it looked at.

236
00:12:07,138 --> 00:12:08,418
After the song.

237
00:12:08,598 --> 00:12:10,838
She stayed against my good side.

238
00:12:11,018 --> 00:12:21,339
The last chorus came. Mercedes’s younger voice caught for half a
breath through the speakers. Onstage, she sang alongside it, smiling.
Porsche stopped laughing to listen.

239
00:12:21,518 --> 00:12:23,198
Shawna leaned to my ear.

240
00:12:23,378 --> 00:12:26,271
Eleven sponsors is a lot of mouths to feed.

241
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,550
I laughed and hurt my shoulder again.

242
00:12:28,730 --> 00:12:31,290
The ticket man opened the door for another group.

243
00:12:31,470 --> 00:12:32,942
Sixty dollars.

244
00:12:33,142 --> 00:12:33,863
I pointed.

245
00:12:34,042 --> 00:12:35,642
Nigga, it was forty!

246
00:12:35,822 --> 00:12:39,262
He nodded toward Mercedes, the man dancing on the coffin, and me.

247
00:12:39,442 --> 00:12:40,914
Live show now.

248
00:12:41,564 --> 00:12:48,364
By the time the police took Silas away, the band had demanded overtime
and Tank was negotiating for the leftover shrimp.

249
00:12:48,544 --> 00:12:56,784
The young sound technician came over with two clean glasses. Twenty-
three, little beard, still looking between Shawna and my DECEASED
wrist stamp.

250
00:12:56,964 --> 00:12:58,264
Can I ask something?

251
00:12:58,464 --> 00:13:00,944
Nigga, apparently you can charge for it.

252
00:13:01,124 --> 00:13:02,306
How’d you two meet?

253
00:13:02,506 --> 00:13:04,986
My wife laughed before I opened my mouth.

254
00:13:05,166 --> 00:13:06,212
Let me tell it,

255
00:13:06,412 --> 00:13:07,372
she said.

256
00:13:07,552 --> 00:13:09,072
Baby, I was there.

257
00:13:09,252 --> 00:13:12,270
So was I. One of us remembers who saved whom.

258
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:14,150
The technician pulled up a chair.

259
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:16,570
Somebody get this nigga a plate,

260
00:13:16,770 --> 00:13:17,570
Tank called.

261
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:18,846
I'm on the clock.

262
00:13:19,046 --> 00:13:22,487
So am I. I organized a death.

263
00:13:22,686 --> 00:13:29,326
Mercedes passed the young man a napkin. Porsche moved the bottle
closer. He loosened the headphones around his neck and sat.

264
00:13:29,506 --> 00:13:34,866
Tank dragged over another chair. Shawna sat against my good side and
took one of the glasses.

265
00:13:35,046 --> 00:13:37,046
I looked at the nigga who had asked.

266
00:13:37,226 --> 00:13:40,186
First night in Vegas. You want the whole thing?

267
00:13:40,366 --> 00:13:41,406
He nodded.

268
00:13:41,586 --> 00:13:43,586
Shawna settled in.

269
00:13:43,766 --> 00:13:45,839
Start before you became reasonable.

270
00:13:46,039 --> 00:13:48,839
Nigga, we still waiting on that chapter.

271
00:13:49,019 --> 00:13:50,619
Tank laughed into his shrimp.

272
00:13:50,799 --> 00:14:01,599
I took a drink. Back then, before any of these niggas knew what we'd
become, the bass was shaking a different wall. Big T had his hand on
my shoulder, and twelve men waited beside the cars.
